  "_note": "The published `lit` tarball is a FOUR-LINE BARREL — it re-exports `lit-element` and `lit-html` and contains no implementation, which is why the package-entry card for `lit` compiles to ~200 bytes and proves almost nothing. The implementation actually shipped to npm lives in the three packages pinned under `implementation`, and those are what this suite compiles. lit's own tests are not in any tarball, so the matching monorepo tag is acquired and its immutable commit verified. The tag `lit@3.3.3` carries lit-html 3.3.3, @lit/reactive-element 2.1.2 and lit-element 4.2.2 — byte-for-byte the versions pinned above, so there is zero version skew between the tests and the implementation under test. testFiles is the ENTIRE `src/test` tree of all three packages (58 files); which of them can be scored is decided at run time and reported by reason, never by hand-picking files here."
